1
00:00:07,625 --> 00:00:09,025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

2
00:01:36,665 --> 00:01:39,025
ADAPTED FROM <i>THE EARLY SPRING</i> ON JJWXC.NET
AUTHOR: GU NIANG BIE KU

3
00:01:44,305 --> 00:01:47,425
From next week,
I'll be stationed in Hong Kong, China.

4
00:01:48,105 --> 00:01:49,145
An assignment from my work.

5
00:01:50,025 --> 00:01:50,985
Hong Kong, China?

6
00:01:51,065 --> 00:01:53,265
That's so sudden. You never mentioned it.

7
00:01:55,145 --> 00:01:56,865
The decision was made last week.

8
00:02:01,145 --> 00:02:05,065
Wang Zhiyong got together
with the new intern.

9
00:02:11,105 --> 00:02:15,585
So, you're leaving because of the breakup?

10
00:02:20,585 --> 00:02:22,225
When you're in your twenties,

11
00:02:23,225 --> 00:02:25,505
you think love is everything.

12
00:02:27,385 --> 00:02:30,185
But the reality
will give you a rude awakening.

13
00:02:30,905 --> 00:02:32,425
A five-year relationship

14
00:02:33,265 --> 00:02:36,985
is nothing compared
to the harshness of life.

15
00:02:41,305 --> 00:02:43,025
I will miss Beijing.

16
00:02:45,385 --> 00:02:47,345
But I think it's not that bad.

17
00:02:49,105 --> 00:02:51,265
Perhaps a new environment

18
00:02:52,225 --> 00:02:56,105
could be the beginning of something new.

19
00:03:03,625 --> 00:03:05,985
When I was packing yesterday,

20
00:03:06,585 --> 00:03:08,705
I found this behind the radiator.

21
00:03:13,945 --> 00:03:15,665
RENT A PLACE WITH FLOOR-TO-CEILING WINDOWS

22
00:03:15,745 --> 00:03:17,225
IN CHAOYANG DISTRICT WITHIN FIVE YEARS!
YAO BEI

23
00:03:18,385 --> 00:03:19,745
Isn't it funny?

24
00:03:26,625 --> 00:03:27,465
Come.

25
00:03:28,905 --> 00:03:29,945
A toast to Beijing.

26
00:03:32,465 --> 00:03:35,345
A toast to when we used to think
love can triumph over property prices.

27
00:03:36,665 --> 00:03:39,305
And now, we know by heart
how to use an Excel sheet

28
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:41,305
to calculate our down payment
and interest.

29
00:03:42,705 --> 00:03:43,905
A toast to Beijing.

30
00:03:45,305 --> 00:03:48,545
A toast to those nights
when we cried and said we couldn't go on.

31
00:03:49,065 --> 00:03:50,505
And when the sun rose,

32
00:03:50,585 --> 00:03:53,345
we still had to save
our presentation slides as a new file.

33
00:03:59,345 --> 00:04:02,425
<i>We learned how to squeeze</i>
<i>into the subway morning rush hour,</i>

34
00:04:02,505 --> 00:04:06,585
<i>and we also learned how to find</i>
<i>our footing amidst the crowd.</i>

35
00:04:07,825 --> 00:04:09,505
INFLUENCER'S PICK, PORK TENDERLOIN 16 YUAN

36
00:04:10,785 --> 00:04:12,465
<i>I want to toast to Beijing too.</i>

37
00:04:13,585 --> 00:04:14,865
To those days

38
00:04:16,865 --> 00:04:18,785
when we cried

39
00:04:19,305 --> 00:04:21,064
and said we wanted
to go home the next day.

40
00:04:22,385 --> 00:04:27,185
Yet when the sun rose,
we swallowed our cold ambition

41
00:04:27,905 --> 00:04:30,145
with a smile.

42
00:04:31,185 --> 00:04:32,025
Shang Zhitao.

43
00:04:32,985 --> 00:04:34,505
You will be fine

44
00:04:35,225 --> 00:04:36,585
because an ambitious person

45
00:04:37,185 --> 00:04:39,265
will not be defeated by life.

46
00:04:44,345 --> 00:04:45,905
We will be invincible.

47
00:04:48,865 --> 00:04:50,145
Come.

48
00:04:57,785 --> 00:05:01,305
AN AMBITIOUS PERSON
WILL NEVER BE DEFEATED BY LIFE

49
00:05:05,465 --> 00:05:07,425
Do you have a history with Luke?

50
00:05:09,065 --> 00:05:10,145
No.

51
00:05:11,465 --> 00:05:13,665
I had to go through a lot to get it.

52
00:05:14,905 --> 00:05:16,065
He didn't ask for anything in return?

53
00:05:17,025 --> 00:05:18,385
He asked me
to do a presentation deck for him.

54
00:05:18,465 --> 00:05:19,385
What for?

55
00:05:20,185 --> 00:05:21,505
I haven't finished it yet.

56
00:05:21,585 --> 00:05:22,545
The automobile company?

57
00:05:27,425 --> 00:05:28,505
Come on.

58
00:05:28,585 --> 00:05:30,705
No need to cover for him.

59
00:05:30,785 --> 00:05:32,665
I already heard his team
has set their eyes on Yueteng Auto.

60
00:05:32,745 --> 00:05:35,745
No wonder he doesn't want Qipai anymore.

61
00:05:36,545 --> 00:05:38,425
You did well. Keep it up.

62
00:05:42,425 --> 00:05:43,585
Go now.

63
00:05:51,025 --> 00:05:52,665
Yueteng…

64
00:05:54,425 --> 00:05:56,905
For the mid-to-low-end customer segment,
you can slightly decrease the budget.

65
00:05:56,985 --> 00:05:58,745
Flora.

66
00:05:59,305 --> 00:06:01,545
You completed the mission impossible.

67
00:06:02,065 --> 00:06:04,025
You are my savior!

68
00:06:05,185 --> 00:06:09,105
But I'm curious.
You managed to impress Luke.

69
00:06:09,185 --> 00:06:10,625
Why did you join us?

70
00:06:11,465 --> 00:06:13,705
I did not impress him.
I couldn't impress him.

71
00:06:14,505 --> 00:06:15,945
Li Tianran, cheer up.

72
00:06:16,545 --> 00:06:17,985
Jealousy is a potion
made with bitter gourd.

73
00:06:18,585 --> 00:06:19,425
It makes your life more bitter.

74
00:06:22,425 --> 00:06:24,625
Regardless, what we want is the result.

75
00:06:25,465 --> 00:06:27,905
Now that we have everything from Qipai,
we can proceed with the rest.

76
00:06:28,825 --> 00:06:30,105
To thank Flora,

77
00:06:30,625 --> 00:06:34,185
the team in charge of Qipai
will have dinner together.

78
00:07:02,425 --> 00:07:04,505
-Sun Yu?
-Hop in.

79
00:07:04,585 --> 00:07:05,545
You…

80
00:07:06,225 --> 00:07:08,305
-Back seat.
-Okay.

81
00:07:08,865 --> 00:07:10,625
-Sit tight.
-Sure.

82
00:07:14,545 --> 00:07:17,465
A COSMIC COINCIDENCE MADE ROMANTIC

83
00:07:17,545 --> 00:07:19,665
Why did you come pick me up today?

84
00:07:19,745 --> 00:07:21,825
Whose car is this? Your company's car?

85
00:07:21,905 --> 00:07:23,065
That's right.

86
00:07:23,145 --> 00:07:26,345
I have been working overtime.
I think I've earned the right

87
00:07:26,425 --> 00:07:28,265
to pick up my friend with my company car.

88
00:07:28,785 --> 00:07:29,905
I'm impressed.

89
00:07:29,985 --> 00:07:33,185
You just got into your new position,
and you got along well with everyone.

90
00:07:33,265 --> 00:07:35,145
A company dinner? Not bad.

91
00:07:36,185 --> 00:07:38,625
Things are picking up right now.

92
00:07:38,705 --> 00:07:39,905
That's good.

93
00:07:41,865 --> 00:07:44,225
Don't. Hide my face.

94
00:07:44,745 --> 00:07:45,785
Let me grab it.

95
00:07:50,265 --> 00:07:51,265
Where are we?

96
00:07:51,345 --> 00:07:53,105
This isn't the right way.

97
00:07:53,865 --> 00:07:57,025
It's not just you.
I also have to pick up Sun as well.

98
00:07:59,065 --> 00:08:00,265
Right.

99
00:08:00,345 --> 00:08:01,305
Pick up Zhu as well.

100
00:08:11,465 --> 00:08:13,305
-Is it cramped back there?
-Very.

101
00:08:13,385 --> 00:08:15,145
I'll get a bigger car
for you guys next time.

102
00:08:15,665 --> 00:08:17,505
How come you're working here today?

103
00:08:18,745 --> 00:08:21,665
My company transferred me
to the self-driving car development team.

104
00:08:21,745 --> 00:08:23,185
They told me
to get a driving license first

105
00:08:23,265 --> 00:08:24,905
so that I could study a driver's habits.

106
00:08:24,985 --> 00:08:26,425
A self-driving car?

107
00:08:26,505 --> 00:08:28,465
Didn't you say you wanted to do that?

108
00:08:28,545 --> 00:08:29,865
This is great.

109
00:08:30,545 --> 00:08:31,705
Driving?

110
00:08:33,185 --> 00:08:34,425
I want to learn how to drive as well.

111
00:08:35,225 --> 00:08:36,264
Sure.

112
00:08:36,784 --> 00:08:38,345
I'll apply through my company.

113
00:08:38,425 --> 00:08:40,945
If you sign up through our company,
you can get a 20% discount.

114
00:08:41,705 --> 00:08:42,904
-Seriously?
-Yes.

115
00:08:42,985 --> 00:08:44,585
Listen. All of you
should get a driving license.

116
00:08:45,105 --> 00:08:48,305
When it's done, all four of us can drive.

117
00:08:49,265 --> 00:08:51,545
The journey of self-improvement
never stops.

118
00:08:51,625 --> 00:08:57,145
That's right. To be more like
the hardworking Tao and the studious Zhu,

119
00:08:57,225 --> 00:08:59,545
I also applied for internal promotion,

120
00:08:59,625 --> 00:09:01,625
so that I can be more like you guys.

121
00:09:02,145 --> 00:09:05,145
I will also work hard
to have a great career.

122
00:09:05,225 --> 00:09:06,065
Good.

123
00:09:06,145 --> 00:09:09,145
Work is tough,
but it also builds character.

124
00:09:09,225 --> 00:09:11,945
Look. Our goals are becoming clearer.

125
00:09:12,025 --> 00:09:13,105
How great is that?

126
00:09:21,265 --> 00:09:23,425
-Come, Mr. Lin.
-Be patient.

127
00:09:23,505 --> 00:09:24,585
Let's wait for Luke.

128
00:09:29,265 --> 00:09:30,265
He's coming as well?

129
00:09:31,185 --> 00:09:33,505
So we'll be talking about…

130
00:09:34,105 --> 00:09:36,865
Have you heard about Yueteng?

131
00:09:39,705 --> 00:09:42,465
As for the Yueteng project, you lost it.

132
00:09:42,545 --> 00:09:44,945
I'm glad Luke managed to win it back.

133
00:09:45,825 --> 00:09:51,225
Don't take this personally
or feel embarrassed.

134
00:09:51,305 --> 00:09:54,025
After all, he gave
Qipai's proposal to you.

135
00:09:54,105 --> 00:09:55,865
We are all one team, aren't we?

136
00:09:56,625 --> 00:09:57,465
Yes.

137
00:09:57,985 --> 00:10:01,425
I've been meaning to thank you in person.

138
00:10:02,025 --> 00:10:05,785
Without your help,
he wouldn't have been this generous.

139
00:10:05,865 --> 00:10:07,185
Not necessarily.

140
00:10:07,705 --> 00:10:10,745
Knowing him, if he truly
didn't want to help you,

141
00:10:10,825 --> 00:10:12,705
he wouldn't have budged,
even if I had leveraged my company

142
00:10:12,785 --> 00:10:13,665
to put pressure on him.

143
00:10:14,705 --> 00:10:16,225
Right.

144
00:10:17,265 --> 00:10:20,985
He always looks down on others
from his pedestal.

145
00:10:21,625 --> 00:10:24,705
Many people in the company
are fed up with his attitude.

146
00:10:27,345 --> 00:10:32,785
But anyway, I did mess up this time.

147
00:10:33,545 --> 00:10:36,345
Luan Nian is a rare talent.

148
00:10:36,425 --> 00:10:37,985
He is capable.

149
00:10:38,585 --> 00:10:40,905
But don't sell yourself short either.

150
00:10:41,425 --> 00:10:42,865
You have your strengths.

151
00:10:43,465 --> 00:10:45,145
This is how Lime works.

152
00:10:45,225 --> 00:10:47,425
We recruit the <i>creme de la creme</i>.

153
00:10:47,505 --> 00:10:48,945
We won't put all our eggs in one basket.

154
00:10:49,545 --> 00:10:51,225
All of you are good at certain things.

155
00:10:51,305 --> 00:10:53,385
That's why our clients
will always come back to us

156
00:10:53,465 --> 00:10:55,945
wherever they go. Right?

157
00:11:00,105 --> 00:11:00,945
Mr. Lin.

158
00:11:01,025 --> 00:11:04,665
Thank you so much.

159
00:11:04,745 --> 00:11:06,945
I am absolutely loyal to you.

160
00:11:07,465 --> 00:11:09,745
I get what you are trying to convey.

161
00:11:10,465 --> 00:11:13,065
I lost Yueteng.

162
00:11:13,145 --> 00:11:14,465
I'm happy for Lime

163
00:11:15,065 --> 00:11:17,745
because he managed to win them back.

164
00:11:18,305 --> 00:11:21,505
If you ever need my assistance
in this project,

165
00:11:22,105 --> 00:11:25,625
I'll drop everything to help out.

166
00:11:26,345 --> 00:11:28,065
Thank you again, Mr. Lin.

167
00:11:31,905 --> 00:11:32,985
Luan Nian, you are here.

168
00:11:33,665 --> 00:11:34,705
Take a seat.

169
00:11:35,225 --> 00:11:37,065
Sorry, Mr. Lin. I'm late.

170
00:11:37,145 --> 00:11:39,945
It's fine. Alex and I
were just talking about Yueteng.

171
00:11:41,745 --> 00:11:46,225
Luke, you sure have avenged me
by winning them back.

172
00:11:46,305 --> 00:11:47,745
My enemy was too weak.

173
00:11:51,065 --> 00:11:52,265
I wasn't talking about you.

174
00:11:52,865 --> 00:11:54,225
I meant the other companies.

175
00:11:54,745 --> 00:11:55,785
It's almost Q4 now,

176
00:11:55,865 --> 00:11:57,785
but they haven't even reached
their KPI for Q2.

177
00:11:59,465 --> 00:12:03,145
While I did get the project back,
I'll need Alex's assistance.

178
00:12:03,225 --> 00:12:06,225
Me? You need my help?

179
00:12:06,305 --> 00:12:08,705
I heard you wined and dined
people from Yueteng's branding department

180
00:12:08,785 --> 00:12:09,625
for nearly six months.

181
00:12:10,385 --> 00:12:13,265
You know their company's
internal project information very well.

182
00:12:13,345 --> 00:12:16,385
-I need that information.
-What are you talking about?

183
00:12:16,465 --> 00:12:17,905
-I…
-Whatever.

184
00:12:19,225 --> 00:12:21,425
Our company needs you two
to work together now.

185
00:12:21,505 --> 00:12:24,705
Yueteng is an important project to Lime.

186
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:28,225
I hope both of you
can prioritize the company's interest.

187
00:12:28,865 --> 00:12:31,265
Luke, you lead the charge.
Alex, you'll support him.

188
00:12:31,865 --> 00:12:33,305
Is that doable or not?

189
00:12:44,865 --> 00:12:45,865
In all seriousness,

190
00:12:46,945 --> 00:12:50,705
I harbor no hostility.
No one is forever the winner in business.

191
00:12:50,785 --> 00:12:53,105
Today, we are enemies.
Tomorrow, we might be allies.

192
00:12:54,065 --> 00:12:58,025
Alex, your effort is not in vain.
You helped us save a lot of time.

193
00:12:58,105 --> 00:13:00,145
Sincere cooperation
is way too formal for us.

194
00:13:00,225 --> 00:13:01,665
Let's make it simple.

195
00:13:01,745 --> 00:13:03,945
We'll split the spoils.

196
00:13:04,665 --> 00:13:05,785
What do you think?

197
00:13:05,865 --> 00:13:06,945
Interested?

198
00:13:13,545 --> 00:13:15,145
Sure.

199
00:13:16,105 --> 00:13:17,145
Luke will take charge.

200
00:13:17,865 --> 00:13:20,265
Make Lime proud, and I'll also feel proud.

201
00:13:21,505 --> 00:13:23,985
May you bring forth the next miracle run

202
00:13:24,065 --> 00:13:26,425
so that Lime continues
to be the biggest player in the industry.

203
00:13:26,505 --> 00:13:27,425
Come.

204
00:13:45,665 --> 00:13:46,625
Nice.

205
00:13:46,705 --> 00:13:47,825
You did it.

206
00:13:47,905 --> 00:13:51,305
You did well, so you've earned
your place in that team.

207
00:13:51,385 --> 00:13:53,705
-You think so?
-Yes.

208
00:13:54,345 --> 00:13:58,065
Without others' help, what should I do
to be allowed into core projects?

209
00:13:58,145 --> 00:14:01,425
Well, stop making Excel sheets for others
like what you are doing now.

210
00:14:01,505 --> 00:14:04,145
That won't earn you
a spot in core projects.

211
00:14:04,785 --> 00:14:08,865
But by studying the data,
I will be familiar with the projects

212
00:14:09,385 --> 00:14:11,505
and how they function.

213
00:14:11,585 --> 00:14:13,225
I know you love to study,

214
00:14:13,305 --> 00:14:16,305
but results speak the loudest at work.

215
00:14:18,225 --> 00:14:20,505
I feel like I can't think straight
during Spring.

216
00:14:20,585 --> 00:14:22,225
I don't feel like working at all.

217
00:14:24,745 --> 00:14:26,345
Flora. Come.

218
00:14:35,625 --> 00:14:37,425
Flora, you did well this time.

219
00:14:38,145 --> 00:14:41,185
Have you had the chance to thank Luke yet?

220
00:14:47,265 --> 00:14:50,065
Thank you, Luke. I'll buy you coffee.

221
00:14:51,225 --> 00:14:53,185
Flora, you are working for Alex now.

222
00:14:54,105 --> 00:14:55,105
Alex should be the one buying.

223
00:14:59,985 --> 00:15:00,865
It's on me.

224
00:15:04,665 --> 00:15:08,225
Lumi, you sure are quick and witty.

225
00:15:09,385 --> 00:15:11,745
Now that both of us will work on Yueteng,

226
00:15:12,825 --> 00:15:15,225
I trust you'll take charge
when it comes to negotiation.

227
00:15:21,145 --> 00:15:22,665
Working on Yueteng together?

228
00:15:29,065 --> 00:15:30,265
I look forward to working together.

229
00:15:37,745 --> 00:15:38,705
Americano.

230
00:15:43,105 --> 00:15:44,065
Alex.

231
00:15:46,305 --> 00:15:47,265
Thank Luke.

232
00:15:54,465 --> 00:15:55,905
-What is going on?
-We'll talk later.

233
00:15:58,345 --> 00:15:59,385
There's an outsider here.

234
00:16:13,145 --> 00:16:14,985
Both teams working on Yueteng?

235
00:16:15,065 --> 00:16:16,425
-Really?
-No idea.

236
00:16:16,505 --> 00:16:17,585
Ask around.

237
00:16:22,745 --> 00:16:23,665
Hello?

238
00:16:24,585 --> 00:16:25,585
Come in.

239
00:16:26,425 --> 00:16:28,505
My parcel. Yes?

240
00:16:30,745 --> 00:16:31,945
-I have no signal.
-What's…

241
00:16:38,505 --> 00:16:41,425
Miss, do you have a bigger one?

242
00:16:41,505 --> 00:16:43,065
How big do you want?

243
00:16:43,145 --> 00:16:44,825
-Will this work?
-Thank you, miss.

244
00:16:44,905 --> 00:16:45,825
You're welcome.

245
00:16:51,545 --> 00:16:52,505
Is this your parcel?

246
00:17:22,385 --> 00:17:23,224
Come with me.

247
00:17:29,945 --> 00:17:31,305
Do you want us to talk here?

248
00:17:48,305 --> 00:17:49,225
Avoiding me?

249
00:17:50,105 --> 00:17:51,145
Am I a ghost or what?

250
00:17:53,825 --> 00:17:54,985
No, I wasn't.

251
00:17:56,985 --> 00:17:59,545
I'm just worried
that you'd threaten to fire me

252
00:17:59,625 --> 00:18:01,265
without giving me an alternative.

253
00:18:02,425 --> 00:18:03,265
Did I do that?

254
00:18:04,905 --> 00:18:07,825
When you wanted the document from me,
you wouldn't leave me alone.

255
00:18:08,345 --> 00:18:09,625
Once you got it,

256
00:18:09,705 --> 00:18:11,225
you kicked me aside.

257
00:18:15,065 --> 00:18:19,385
I wish to maintain
a professional distance between us.

258
00:18:19,905 --> 00:18:23,585
I can reassure you
that I am not an ungrateful person.

259
00:18:25,105 --> 00:18:27,745
I am very grateful
that you lent me your help.

260
00:18:28,265 --> 00:18:31,585
If you ever need my assistance,

261
00:18:33,225 --> 00:18:35,585
-I'll help out--
-Why would I ever need your assistance?

262
00:18:41,145 --> 00:18:43,025
I am not inferior to others.

263
00:18:44,145 --> 00:18:47,505
If you need me,
I'll do my best to help you,

264
00:18:47,585 --> 00:18:50,265
but please stop threatening me
with dismissal.

265
00:18:50,345 --> 00:18:51,825
I can't bear it.

266
00:18:57,185 --> 00:18:58,065
Shang Zhitao.

267
00:19:02,905 --> 00:19:04,465
You are so timid,

268
00:19:05,265 --> 00:19:06,665
shy, humble, and sheepish.

269
00:19:08,065 --> 00:19:09,905
How can you survive in this industry?

270
00:19:11,545 --> 00:19:13,505
And you said
you were not inferior to others?

271
00:19:21,465 --> 00:19:23,225
I think you're being inappropriate.

272
00:19:26,705 --> 00:19:28,625
Haven't we made it clear?

273
00:19:31,665 --> 00:19:32,745
It was an accident.

274
00:19:36,945 --> 00:19:38,785
Can't you control the feeling of love?

275
00:19:41,905 --> 00:19:42,945
The feeling of love…

276
00:19:46,065 --> 00:19:47,025
can be controlled.

277
00:20:29,385 --> 00:20:30,905
Come here, everyone.

278
00:20:34,745 --> 00:20:37,385
I have a good announcement to make.

279
00:20:37,465 --> 00:20:39,625
Mr. Lin. After you.

280
00:20:42,345 --> 00:20:43,905
I have good news.

281
00:20:44,545 --> 00:20:48,225
Luke managed to win Yueteng Auto back.

282
00:20:56,545 --> 00:20:57,385
Thank you.

283
00:20:57,985 --> 00:21:00,305
Yueteng is our key client this year.

284
00:21:01,025 --> 00:21:04,865
Moving forward, Alex and I
will be assembling a new project team

285
00:21:04,945 --> 00:21:06,465
from both our teams.

286
00:21:07,065 --> 00:21:08,065
I ask for your cooperation.

287
00:21:09,425 --> 00:21:12,985
We only won them back this time
because our opponent, Chengbiao,

288
00:21:13,065 --> 00:21:14,225
picked the wrong printing company.

289
00:21:14,905 --> 00:21:18,825
In the future, we must carefully vet
and pick out the right supplier.

290
00:21:19,385 --> 00:21:23,425
And I want your teams
to submit the list of suppliers to me.

291
00:21:23,505 --> 00:21:24,985
We will go through them together.

292
00:21:25,065 --> 00:21:28,985
Of course, you may also
recommend any suppliers.

293
00:21:31,425 --> 00:21:32,425
Alex.

294
00:21:33,385 --> 00:21:35,105
Anything you'd like to add?

295
00:21:35,185 --> 00:21:37,945
Nothing. We'll follow you.

296
00:21:38,945 --> 00:21:41,625
Luke, you never let us down.

297
00:21:42,145 --> 00:21:43,585
And Alex, you are also a great leader.

298
00:21:44,305 --> 00:21:47,745
It puts my mind at ease that both of you
are running Lime China.

299
00:22:08,585 --> 00:22:11,385
Zhang Ling. Are you out of your mind?

300
00:22:12,145 --> 00:22:13,545
You kept those people entertained

301
00:22:13,625 --> 00:22:15,505
for three months
before you got that information.

302
00:22:16,025 --> 00:22:17,425
And now, you're giving them to Luan Nian?

303
00:22:18,545 --> 00:22:20,145
It was Mr. Lin's decision.

304
00:22:20,225 --> 00:22:22,905
Besides, we took his project, didn't we?

305
00:22:23,505 --> 00:22:24,345
We're even now.

306
00:22:25,865 --> 00:22:28,625
Mr. Lin only sees Luan Nian.

307
00:22:28,705 --> 00:22:31,265
No matter what we've done
or how well we've done,

308
00:22:31,345 --> 00:22:32,905
he never acknowledges it.

309
00:22:33,785 --> 00:22:35,265
Luan Nian never lets anyone down?

310
00:22:39,625 --> 00:22:41,505
Oh, and you're a great leader too.

311
00:22:43,105 --> 00:22:46,865
So tell me, great leader,
what do we do next?

312
00:22:47,505 --> 00:22:49,145
Help Luan Nian achieve his ambition?

313
00:22:50,985 --> 00:22:54,265
Come on. It's not that bad.

314
00:22:58,225 --> 00:22:59,545
Listen.

315
00:22:59,625 --> 00:23:01,145
Luan Nian is not a friend.

316
00:23:01,985 --> 00:23:04,825
When he gets promoted, you'll regret it.

317
00:23:20,745 --> 00:23:21,705
<i>There's an update.</i>

318
00:23:21,785 --> 00:23:23,705
Yueteng wants to change
its marketing strategy

319
00:23:23,785 --> 00:23:25,665
to digital marketing.

320
00:23:25,745 --> 00:23:28,185
I need the data of major suppliers.

321
00:23:28,265 --> 00:23:29,305
Who can do it?

322
00:23:30,425 --> 00:23:35,585
In our line of work, there isn't
a standardized database.

323
00:23:35,665 --> 00:23:38,145
Just because it's the status quo
doesn't mean it's right.

324
00:23:40,065 --> 00:23:42,065
We all have different suppliers

325
00:23:42,145 --> 00:23:44,025
because we work on different projects.

326
00:23:44,105 --> 00:23:45,745
Then, tell me.

327
00:23:46,305 --> 00:23:49,745
Among your suppliers,
who is the most competent?

328
00:23:50,585 --> 00:23:51,785
Who is the most cooperative?

329
00:23:51,865 --> 00:23:53,985
Who can advance us the longest?

330
00:23:54,585 --> 00:23:56,105
What is the maximum amount?

331
00:23:56,185 --> 00:23:58,305
What is their respective expertise?

332
00:24:02,825 --> 00:24:03,665
Who can do it?

333
00:24:04,905 --> 00:24:06,065
I can do it.

334
00:24:06,625 --> 00:24:09,105
But I need someone
who is good at Excel to assist me.

335
00:24:10,025 --> 00:24:11,625
I… I can assist you.

336
00:24:15,105 --> 00:24:16,945
Okay. You'll do it.

337
00:24:17,545 --> 00:24:20,425
On top of compiling the list
of major suppliers, we can include

338
00:24:20,505 --> 00:24:22,145
new suppliers with potential.

339
00:24:22,745 --> 00:24:24,785
Compile everything
and put it in the database.

340
00:24:24,865 --> 00:24:27,625
Our management needs
to be professional and systematic.

341
00:24:27,705 --> 00:24:31,105
Only a systematic method
can lead us in the right direction

342
00:24:32,025 --> 00:24:33,625
and prevent some financial problems.

343
00:24:38,945 --> 00:24:39,985
Of course.

344
00:24:41,105 --> 00:24:42,945
Let's all work together.

345
00:24:50,705 --> 00:24:53,745
Luke wants us to quantify the maximum
advance period and company reputation

346
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:55,425
into a grading scheme.

347
00:24:55,505 --> 00:24:57,945
That will expedite
the subsequent operation.

348
00:24:58,025 --> 00:25:02,025
Our Business Division has changed
four supplier systems within three years.

349
00:25:02,665 --> 00:25:03,985
In the end, they become scrap paper.

350
00:25:04,705 --> 00:25:07,705
The major suppliers in the market
are not lacking in work,

351
00:25:07,785 --> 00:25:09,385
and the Yueteng project
is on a tight deadline.

352
00:25:10,025 --> 00:25:11,985
Instead of cutting down
the turnaround time,

353
00:25:12,065 --> 00:25:13,905
we have to come up
with a supplier database.

354
00:25:14,425 --> 00:25:15,265
Foolish.

355
00:25:17,145 --> 00:25:19,665
If you want to be foolhardy, be my guest.

356
00:25:19,745 --> 00:25:22,225
I have work to do.
Go to Li Tianran if you need help.

357
00:25:22,745 --> 00:25:26,945
Flora, perhaps you can get clearance
from IT first?

358
00:25:27,545 --> 00:25:29,705
Do you have access to confidential data?

359
00:25:48,705 --> 00:25:50,625
I was too reckless
in the meeting just now.

360
00:25:50,705 --> 00:25:52,145
I was too focused
on bringing you on board.

361
00:25:52,905 --> 00:25:55,825
This task is tough.

362
00:25:56,585 --> 00:25:58,265
I have already experienced it firsthand.

363
00:25:59,105 --> 00:26:00,905
But I agree with Luke.

364
00:26:00,985 --> 00:26:02,865
The market needs fairness and a system.

365
00:26:03,545 --> 00:26:07,225
I'm familiar with analytics.
I can make the supplier database.

366
00:26:08,745 --> 00:26:10,585
I see you've learned
a lot as the Excel sheet girl.

367
00:26:11,185 --> 00:26:15,625
I bet your knowledge of Excel sheets
is among the top five in our company.

368
00:26:15,705 --> 00:26:18,665
And the top four
are those geniuses in business analysis.

369
00:26:19,585 --> 00:26:22,865
I just think knowing it
makes me more efficient.

370
00:26:23,865 --> 00:26:25,065
And you are right.

371
00:26:27,865 --> 00:26:28,785
You know what?

372
00:26:28,865 --> 00:26:31,145
I'll compile the data on suppliers.

373
00:26:31,225 --> 00:26:33,025
I'm not afraid of anything.

374
00:26:33,105 --> 00:26:35,185
If they don't cooperate,
I'll spit on them.

375
00:26:35,785 --> 00:26:37,265
And you…

376
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:40,385
Go to Luke and ask what he truly wants.

377
00:26:41,625 --> 00:26:42,545
I…

378
00:26:42,625 --> 00:26:43,785
Me?

379
00:26:44,465 --> 00:26:46,025
What's there to be afraid of?

380
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:47,345
You're working for him.

381
00:26:47,425 --> 00:26:49,065
What is he going to do? Eat you?

382
00:26:50,265 --> 00:26:53,345
He's very serious when it comes to work.
He won't make things difficult for you.

383
00:26:53,425 --> 00:26:54,425
Okay?

384
00:27:06,145 --> 00:27:07,425
Come in.

385
00:27:10,385 --> 00:27:11,225
Luke.

386
00:27:12,185 --> 00:27:13,185
Are you busy?

387
00:27:14,385 --> 00:27:15,385
Yes.

388
00:27:16,025 --> 00:27:16,945
Busy avoiding rumors.

389
00:27:20,825 --> 00:27:22,465
I need to ask you something.

390
00:27:25,105 --> 00:27:25,985
Don't close the door.

391
00:27:37,545 --> 00:27:38,265
Speak.

392
00:27:38,345 --> 00:27:41,145
You mentioned making
a supplier database today.

393
00:27:41,225 --> 00:27:42,785
What is the aim of this exercise?

394
00:27:44,985 --> 00:27:48,065
To build an internal
grading scheme for good suppliers.

395
00:27:48,145 --> 00:27:50,825
Engagement and termination
of suppliers need a system.

396
00:27:50,905 --> 00:27:52,505
Just like when you were studying.

397
00:27:53,065 --> 00:27:55,345
There's a passing grade.
There's a grade for resitting.

398
00:27:55,425 --> 00:27:58,065
When you fall below a certain grade,
you will be expelled.

399
00:27:58,145 --> 00:27:59,985
We cannot be leashed by suppliers.

400
00:28:00,065 --> 00:28:01,385
Our clients all need major suppliers.

401
00:28:02,025 --> 00:28:04,025
If the major suppliers
do not work with us for the evaluation,

402
00:28:04,105 --> 00:28:06,265
we'll make one.

403
00:28:06,945 --> 00:28:08,305
I don't quite follow.

404
00:28:08,385 --> 00:28:10,625
Identify suppliers with good potential

405
00:28:10,705 --> 00:28:14,585
and tell them that I can help them
expand their business

406
00:28:14,665 --> 00:28:15,905
by acquiring smaller companies.

407
00:28:15,985 --> 00:28:17,705
Once the Yueteng project concludes,

408
00:28:17,785 --> 00:28:20,105
they will naturally be the top supplier.

409
00:28:21,465 --> 00:28:22,465
I see.

410
00:28:23,305 --> 00:28:26,585
The market needs fairness.
Big companies need checks and balances.

411
00:28:26,665 --> 00:28:28,185
Small companies need opportunities.

412
00:28:31,625 --> 00:28:33,265
It is a monumental task.

413
00:28:33,865 --> 00:28:37,465
If you join us, you won't be able
to join other projects for a while,

414
00:28:37,985 --> 00:28:38,905
and you'll cross a lot of people.

415
00:28:39,585 --> 00:28:40,865
-You can choose to--
-Worry not.

416
00:28:41,465 --> 00:28:42,865
It will be done.

417
00:28:44,705 --> 00:28:45,545
Okay.

418
00:28:46,145 --> 00:28:47,745
Come to me if you have any questions.

419
00:28:49,105 --> 00:28:50,785
I would like to apply
for clearance from IT.

420
00:28:50,865 --> 00:28:53,465
I do not have access to confidential data.

421
00:28:56,305 --> 00:28:57,905
Submit the application,
and I'll approve it.

422
00:28:58,945 --> 00:29:00,065
Thanks, Luke.

423
00:29:01,185 --> 00:29:02,025
Flora.

424
00:29:04,785 --> 00:29:07,585
You're bolder than I imagined.

425
00:29:08,385 --> 00:29:09,705
And smarter too.

426
00:29:14,185 --> 00:29:15,505
I will continue to work hard.

427
00:29:22,825 --> 00:29:25,065
You can have this. Thank you, Luke.

428
00:30:08,105 --> 00:30:08,945
<i>Sun Yu.</i>

429
00:30:09,025 --> 00:30:11,225
<i>I have to verify</i>
<i>supplier qualifications today.</i>

430
00:30:11,305 --> 00:30:13,945
-<i>I'll be back late.</i>
-<i>Okay. Got it.</i>

431
00:30:14,025 --> 00:30:15,665
TIANTONGYUAN STATION SUBWAY SCHEDULE

432
00:30:15,745 --> 00:30:17,025
CHINA LIFE - CP CENTER

433
00:30:17,105 --> 00:30:18,225
SERVICE QUALITY CERTIFICATION

434
00:30:22,065 --> 00:30:22,945
A HIGH DEGREE OF SIMILARITY
IS OBSERVED ACROSS CREATIVE PROPOSALS

435
00:30:23,025 --> 00:30:23,985
OVERALL SCORE 8.3/10

436
00:30:49,825 --> 00:30:52,385
SUPPLIER GRADING SCHEME HEADER

437
00:31:12,225 --> 00:31:14,425
Tao. What happened to your foot?

438
00:31:14,505 --> 00:31:15,945
I'm such a rookie
when it comes to on-the-ground surveys.

439
00:31:16,025 --> 00:31:17,745
My high heels gave me blisters.

440
00:31:17,825 --> 00:31:20,585
-I'm fine.
-Why didn't you wear sneakers?

441
00:31:20,665 --> 00:31:24,225
Tell them you work at Lime.
You look good in anything.

442
00:31:24,305 --> 00:31:25,145
I'll be more mindful next time.

443
00:31:26,225 --> 00:31:27,185
How did the survey go?

444
00:31:27,785 --> 00:31:31,065
I went to many places today.
Less than half got the passing grade.

445
00:31:32,145 --> 00:31:33,985
He truly made the right call.

446
00:31:35,305 --> 00:31:36,665
At this point, just go back and rest.

447
00:31:36,745 --> 00:31:38,265
I'll go back later.

448
00:31:38,345 --> 00:31:42,905
I have a senior, and I got the supplier
grading scheme header from her company.

449
00:31:42,985 --> 00:31:45,385
I'll sort and organize it later.

450
00:31:45,465 --> 00:31:47,225
It's good to work hard,
but don't overwork yourself.

451
00:31:48,105 --> 00:31:49,065
Go home early.

452
00:32:03,145 --> 00:32:04,665
SUPPLIER GRADING SCHEME HEADER

453
00:32:04,745 --> 00:32:05,985
LIST OF SUPPLIERS

454
00:32:51,945 --> 00:32:55,985
<i>If talented people already work this hard,</i>
<i>I have to work harder to keep up.</i>

455
00:33:31,585 --> 00:33:32,305
LUAN NIAN

456
00:33:32,385 --> 00:33:33,585
<i>It'll rain soon.</i>

457
00:33:33,665 --> 00:33:34,705
<i>Let me drive you home.</i>

458
00:33:40,465 --> 00:33:44,065
<i>Thanks. But I haven't finished</i>
<i>my work yet. Just go first.</i>

459
00:33:49,425 --> 00:33:50,585
<i>Kicking me aside again?</i>

460
00:33:58,705 --> 00:33:59,705
<i>I'm waiting for you at the parking lot.</i>

461
00:34:11,744 --> 00:34:13,145
LIST OF SUPPLIERS

462
00:34:18,385 --> 00:34:19,545
What happened to your foot?

463
00:34:20,065 --> 00:34:22,105
I didn't wear comfortable shoes today.

464
00:34:22,185 --> 00:34:23,744
You didn't wear something comfortable
to conduct surveys?

465
00:34:24,625 --> 00:34:25,744
I'll be mindful next time.

466
00:34:28,465 --> 00:34:30,905
-How is the list going?
-Still compiling it.

467
00:34:31,985 --> 00:34:34,784
Go to HR tomorrow
and apply for overtime pay.

468
00:34:34,865 --> 00:34:36,824
Submit it online,
and put me down as the approver.

469
00:34:37,705 --> 00:34:39,705
I can get overtime pay?

470
00:34:40,304 --> 00:34:41,185
Is that a surprise?

471
00:34:42,264 --> 00:34:43,545
What is the rate?

472
00:34:43,625 --> 00:34:45,344
Per second.

473
00:34:49,665 --> 00:34:50,505
You actually believed me?

474
00:34:52,185 --> 00:34:53,025
Yeah.

475
00:34:55,025 --> 00:34:58,625
Oh, Luke. I have a question.

476
00:34:58,705 --> 00:35:00,785
How come no one
has made this database before?

477
00:35:00,865 --> 00:35:03,585
Can I offset the tuition fee
with your overtime pay?

478
00:35:05,945 --> 00:35:07,345
I'll ask you again tomorrow.

479
00:35:11,225 --> 00:35:13,345
The fiercer the competition is,
the more profitable it is.

480
00:35:14,025 --> 00:35:15,505
The first one always gets
the biggest slice of the cake,

481
00:35:15,585 --> 00:35:16,705
while the rest get crumbs.

482
00:35:16,785 --> 00:35:20,305
A strict yardstick is mandatory
for future systematic management.

483
00:35:23,345 --> 00:35:24,425
I see.

484
00:35:27,545 --> 00:35:29,345
SUN YUANZHU

485
00:35:30,665 --> 00:35:31,505
Hello?

486
00:35:31,585 --> 00:35:32,785
<i>It's going to rain tonight.</i>

487
00:35:32,865 --> 00:35:34,985
-<i>I'll pick you up.</i>
-No need.

488
00:35:35,665 --> 00:35:37,105
I'm on my way home.

489
00:36:20,785 --> 00:36:22,745
Thank you, Luke. I've troubled you again.

490
00:37:24,785 --> 00:37:25,825
I'll walk you up.

491
00:37:30,705 --> 00:37:31,705
I can do it myself.

492
00:37:32,865 --> 00:37:34,025
Thank you.

493
00:37:39,225 --> 00:37:40,105
Tao.

494
00:37:43,105 --> 00:37:44,345
You're here.

495
00:37:44,865 --> 00:37:45,945
Didn't I tell you no need to pick me up?

496
00:37:47,785 --> 00:37:49,945
But the road conditions
might be bad when it rains.

497
00:37:50,025 --> 00:37:51,225
I'm coming over.

498
00:37:52,985 --> 00:37:54,025
Don't get wet in the rain.

499
00:37:54,105 --> 00:37:55,865
-You'll catch a cold.
-Okay.

500
00:37:57,345 --> 00:37:59,185
Thanks, Luke. We'll be going now.

501
00:38:00,025 --> 00:38:00,985
Come.

502
00:38:01,585 --> 00:38:02,785
What's with your foot?

503
00:38:02,865 --> 00:38:04,825
-The new shoes hurt my feet.
-Does it hurt?

504
00:38:06,065 --> 00:38:07,265
Careful.

505
00:38:35,065 --> 00:38:36,665
Can't you control the feeling of love?

506
00:38:39,105 --> 00:38:40,105
The feeling of love…

507
00:38:43,225 --> 00:38:44,145
can be controlled.

508
00:38:56,905 --> 00:38:57,745
Hello?

509
00:38:57,825 --> 00:38:58,665
<i>Son.</i>

510
00:38:58,745 --> 00:39:01,025
<i>Ms. Liu has arranged</i>
<i>for you to meet that girl.</i>

511
00:39:01,105 --> 00:39:03,025
<i>Does Friday night work for you?</i>

512
00:39:03,545 --> 00:39:05,465
Tell Ms. Liu there's no need
to arrange the meeting.

513
00:39:05,985 --> 00:39:06,985
What?

514
00:39:08,465 --> 00:39:11,945
Didn't you just say you would meet her?

515
00:39:12,025 --> 00:39:12,865
What happened?

516
00:39:15,105 --> 00:39:17,745
What I said just now was just
for the moment. Now it's different.

517
00:39:18,385 --> 00:39:19,265
You…

518
00:39:22,705 --> 00:39:25,825
You know I never like
to meddle in your private life.

519
00:39:26,945 --> 00:39:29,145
<i>The reason we arranged</i>
<i>this blind date for you</i>

520
00:39:29,225 --> 00:39:32,545
<i>is that it's hard to refuse such</i>
<i>a kind offer from friends and relatives.</i>

521
00:39:33,145 --> 00:39:35,265
Ms. Liu doesn't know
that you have a bad temper

522
00:39:35,345 --> 00:39:36,265
and a weird personality.

523
00:39:36,865 --> 00:39:38,585
<i>She loves your pretty face, that's all.</i>

524
00:39:39,665 --> 00:39:41,945
<i>Anyway, it's okay</i>
<i>if you don't want to meet her.</i>

525
00:39:42,465 --> 00:39:44,305
<i>That will tell her</i>

526
00:39:44,985 --> 00:39:46,625
how intolerable you are.

527
00:39:47,385 --> 00:39:48,705
<i>Even if you date her,</i>

528
00:39:48,785 --> 00:39:51,505
<i>I'm sure she can't put up</i>
<i>with you for more than a few days.</i>

529
00:39:51,585 --> 00:39:54,785
<i>Let's not waste her favor</i>
<i>and hurt the girl.</i>

530
00:40:26,345 --> 00:40:27,265
What's so funny?

531
00:40:28,425 --> 00:40:30,185
-I have a question.
-Go ahead.

532
00:40:31,705 --> 00:40:33,225
Am I intolerable?

533
00:40:35,265 --> 00:40:36,545
What do you think?

534
00:40:36,625 --> 00:40:39,705
Other than your mom or your few friends,
who can tolerate your antics?

535
00:40:41,905 --> 00:40:43,945
I thought you didn't want love.

536
00:40:44,705 --> 00:40:46,545
Look at you.

537
00:40:47,865 --> 00:40:49,825
Did you confess
to someone and get rejected?

538
00:40:50,665 --> 00:40:52,705
Girls nowadays don't care
about casual flings.

539
00:40:53,225 --> 00:40:54,345
They want to be independent.

540
00:40:55,065 --> 00:40:56,305
They want a career, not a relationship.

541
00:41:00,425 --> 00:41:01,945
I beg to differ.

542
00:41:02,465 --> 00:41:06,065
I think Ms. Shang is quite special to you.

543
00:41:07,665 --> 00:41:09,385
She broke the window with her bare hands
to save you on that stormy night.

544
00:41:09,465 --> 00:41:10,905
Has she ever asked for any compensation?

545
00:41:12,025 --> 00:41:14,945
She fixed your typewriter.
Isn't that genuine kindness?

546
00:41:15,025 --> 00:41:18,345
Everyone wants romantic love.
Unless they are an idiot.

547
00:41:18,425 --> 00:41:21,425
What she doesn't like is the way you think
money can solve everything.

548
00:41:21,505 --> 00:41:22,705
That's not a good attitude.

549
00:41:25,185 --> 00:41:27,225
We express ourselves differently.

550
00:41:28,185 --> 00:41:30,625
Besides, wasn't it your idea
to buy her a gift?

551
00:41:36,305 --> 00:41:38,865
I told you to water a plant,
not drown it with hot water.

552
00:41:39,785 --> 00:41:43,745
I told you to buy her a gift
to show some gratitude.

553
00:41:43,825 --> 00:41:45,705
You made it look like
you were compensating for her loss.

554
00:41:45,785 --> 00:41:48,505
You might as well treat her to <i>malatang</i>.

555
00:41:49,425 --> 00:41:51,945
You are a typical case
of wanting something but being scared.

556
00:41:52,785 --> 00:41:54,265
You don't want her to cling to you,

557
00:41:54,945 --> 00:41:56,105
yet you are afraid
that she doesn't care about you.

558
00:41:56,705 --> 00:41:57,505
Mr. Luan,

559
00:41:58,585 --> 00:41:59,745
you have lost it.

560
00:42:19,505 --> 00:42:21,305
SUN YUANZHU

561
00:42:22,665 --> 00:42:23,505
Hi, hello?

562
00:42:23,585 --> 00:42:24,745
<i>It's going to rain tonight.</i>

563
00:42:24,825 --> 00:42:26,945
-<i>I'll pick you up.</i>
-No need.

564
00:42:27,545 --> 00:42:29,145
I'm on my way home.

565
00:42:30,665 --> 00:42:31,745
-Bye.
-<i>Bye.</i>

566
00:42:42,585 --> 00:42:44,705
DR. LIANG

567
00:42:46,225 --> 00:42:47,465
Mom.

568
00:42:47,545 --> 00:42:50,305
<i>Ms. Liu has arranged</i>
<i>for you to meet that girl.</i>

569
00:42:50,385 --> 00:42:52,745
<i>When are you going to be free?</i>

570
00:42:52,825 --> 00:42:54,065
<i>Listen.</i>

571
00:42:54,145 --> 00:42:57,945
<i>I don't care if you date her or not.</i>
<i>We just have to return the courtesy.</i>

572
00:42:58,465 --> 00:43:02,265
<i>Just meet her once</i>
<i>and don't humiliate her.</i>

573
00:43:03,945 --> 00:43:04,905
A blind date?

574
00:43:05,545 --> 00:43:07,385
I'm free this week. Just let me know when.

575
00:43:08,065 --> 00:43:10,025
<i>Really? Sure.</i>

576
00:43:10,105 --> 00:43:10,945
<i>I'll arrange for it then.</i>

577
00:43:12,225 --> 00:43:13,185
Bye.

578
00:43:24,145 --> 00:43:25,185
Have you been on a blind date?

579
00:43:26,225 --> 00:43:27,065
No.

580
00:43:28,745 --> 00:43:32,305
I think it's great. You can find
someone of your social standing.

581
00:43:32,905 --> 00:43:34,145
It's safer.

